# Initiate AI Engineering Workbench

When a session starts in this repo, or the user opens a new enquiry, **orient first**.
Do not answer repository-state questions from memory alone.

## What this repo is

Engineering productivity and knowledge orchestration hub.
Not a bot that sends messages. Humans review and copy/paste every external reply.

## Wire the agent stack

| Layer | Canonical path | Role |
|-------|----------------|------|
| System instructions | `.github/copilot-instructions.md` | Operating defaults, output shape, knowledge nav |
| Agent behaviour | `AGENTS.md` | Mission, truth hierarchy, investigation rules |
| Prompts | `prompts/` (also `.github/prompts/`) | Task templates |
| Skills | `.github/skills/` | Reusable skill definitions |
| Cursor rules | `.cursor/rules/` | Always-on policy |
| Knowledge | `knowledge/` | Registry, architecture, services, integrations |
| Living context | `context/` | Sprint, incidents, investigations, decisions |
| Workflows | `workflows/` | End-to-end playbooks |
| Start CLI | `scripts/start.sh` via `npm run start` | Bootstrap enquiry reports |

## Session bootstrap

1. Skim `AGENTS.md` + `.github/copilot-instructions.md`.
2. Open `knowledge/service-registry.yaml`.
3. Check `knowledge/local-repos.md` and sibling checkouts.
4. Skim `context/` for urgency constraints.
5. Pick matching `prompts/*.md` and `workflows/*.md`.
6. Only then inspect live repos/PRs. Workbench docs navigate; live state decides.

## Hard boundaries

- Do not send Chat/email/Jira/Slack.
- Do not invent PRs, tickets, dates, or deploy status.
- Do not modify other repos unless explicitly instructed.
- Never add `Co-authored-by` on commits.

## Ready check

You are ready when you can name: the prompt/workflow in use, affected services from the registry, whether evidence will come from sibling checkouts and/or `gh`, and that the human will send any external reply.
